"""Single prepared-state policy, identical for all sources and models."""
import json
from .document_policy import GUIDE as ORIGINAL_GUIDE,prepare_inputs,prepare_action
VERSION='prepared-layers-v14-dev2'
GUIDE=ORIGINAL_GUIDE.replace(
'{"op":"unfold"} physically opens your latest retained fold in forward time, preserving plastic material history. This is NOT undo. Paper turns update the stored fold axis. Folds must be unfolded in reverse application order.',
'{"op":"unfold"} physically opens the latest active fold in forward time. Or {"op":"unfold","fold_id":3,"angle_deg":90} opens a specified active fold by a positive angle up to its remaining angle. Omitting angle opens it fully. Earlier folds can open while later, disjoint folds remain; overlapping dependent folds must open first, and physical contact may still block an independent fold. Partial unfolding retains the fold ID. This is NOT undo and preserves plastic history. Paper turns update the stored axes. Active fold IDs and their past commands are public.')
GUIDE+='\nFor a packet of multiple upper or lower layers use layers={"side":"top","count":2} or side="bottom" with a positive integer count. Layers are ordered at moving_point; choose a point through the intended packet. This moves exactly that many connected panels, and rejects if the point does not intersect enough layers. A diagram may call a folded packet a top flap or layer even when it contains multiple physical panels. Infer its packet size from the paper and past folds. Count is not inferred from the diagram by the simulator.'
GUIDE+='\nThe task starts from an already prepared paper state. Its past preparation commands are disclosed and were executed physically; they are not your attempts. Begin at the requested diagram scope. Undo cannot go before this starting state. You may physically unfold a preparation fold. Remaining angles and IDs describe past actions, not private goals. No future reference actions are exposed.'
GUIDE+='\nFollow the illustrated intermediate states in order as well as the final shape. Different action decompositions are allowed, but skipping a demonstrated fold-and-open sequence is not full diagram completion. The private shape checks and their progress are never shown during the episode.'
def prompt(obs):
 return GUIDE+'\nPUBLIC STATE: '+json.dumps(dict(task=obs['task'],document=obs['document'],paper_state_hash=obs['current']['state_hash'],preparation_actions=obs['preparation_actions'],active_folds=obs['active_folds'],retained_paper_actions=obs['accepted_actions'],last_result=obs['previous_action_result'],history=obs['attempt_history'],budget=obs['attempt_budget']),ensure_ascii=False)
